\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Validation on 1815 radiative transfer models that were not used to fit the relation of Eq.~(\ref {eq:law}). Total: the surface density summed over the footprint of the model, divided by the true value. Core mass: the same sum less the background, divided by the same measurement on the true image. Center and $21{\ensuremath  {^{\prime \prime }}}$: the relative residual of the surface density at 3 and $21{\ensuremath  {^{\prime \prime }}}$ from the center of the core. The rows give the image before the correction and after it, with the factor evaluated on the image at $36.3{\ensuremath  {^{\prime \prime }}}$ or at $13.5{\ensuremath  {^{\prime \prime }}}$. The first two columns give the median over the models, with the 16th and 84th percentiles in parentheses; the last two give medians.}}{7}{table.2}\protected@file@percent }
